Chapter: VecLaneComputedOob
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 The lane here is COMPUTED, so CDX2093 cannot see it -- that refusal reads
 literals, and `1 + 1` is not one. This is the case the static check leaves
 open by construction, and it is why the runtime guard exists beside it.

 Before the guard this scaled the index, added it to the vector's base and
 loaded, so lane 2 of a two-lane vector read the eight bytes after it.

 Written with `1 + 1` rather than a bare `2` deliberately: a bare 2 would
 be refused at CHECK and this file would then be testing the wrong guard
 while looking like it tested this one.

 `.fatal`: dies on UD2. The battery-visible half is
 codex/test/ops/vec-lanes-smoke.codex, which reads both legal lanes
 through a computed index and must keep working.

Section: Entry

  pick : Integer -> Real
  pick (i) = vec-extract (vec-splat 1.5) i

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (show (pick (1 + 1)))
  end

